## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical use of caching to reduce Cosmos DB read latency and RU consumption while maintaining strict per-tenant isolation. Evaluates end-to-end system thinking, including invalidation strategies, key schema design, and deployment considerations across environments.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant cache key schema and TTL configuration
- Cache-aside pattern with selective invalidation
- Event-driven cache invalidation via Event Grid
- Observability: cache hit rate, latency metrics, and eviction counts
- Environment isolation: separate Redis instances for dev/stage/prod

## Code Example
```javascript
function redisKey(tenantId, method, path, query) {
  const queryHash = hashQueryString(query);
  return `${tenantId}:${method}:${path}:${queryHash}`;
}

async function getCachedOrFetch(ctx, tenantId, method, path, query) {
  const key = redisKey(tenantId, method, path, query);
  const cached = await redis.get(key);
  if (cached) return JSON.parse(cached);

  const result = await cosmosQuery(tenantId, path, query);
  await redis.setex(key, 300, JSON.stringify(result));
  return result;
}

async function invalidateTenantCache(tenantId) {
  const pattern = `${tenantId}:*`;
  for await (const key of redis.scanIterator({ match: pattern })) {
    await redis.del(key);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Evaluate ability to implement observability across heterogeneous runtimes in Azure, with end-to-end tracing and cross-service propagation.

## Key Concepts
- OpenTelemetry across Functions, AKS, Databricks
- W3C TraceContext; OTLP exporting to Azure Monitor
- Context propagation through queues and Delta Lake
- Sampling strategies and trace retention

## Code Example
```javascript
const { trace, context, propagation } = require('@opentelemetry/api');
const { NodeTracerProvider } = require('@opentelemetry/sdk-trace-node');
const { SimpleSpanProcessor } = require('@opentelemetry/sdk-trace-base');
const { OTLPTraceExporter } = require('@opentelemetry/exporter-otlp-http');

const provider = new NodeTracerProvider();
const exporter = new OTLPTraceExporter({ url: 'https://<region>.monitor.azure.com/v1/traces' });
provider.addSpanProcessor(new SimpleSpanProcessor(exporter));
provider.register();

module.exports = async function (context, req) {
  const tracer = trace.getTracer('example-function');
  const span = tracer.startSpan('http-request');
  // downstream calls propagate context automatically when using OpenTelemetry API
  span.end();
  return { status: 200, body: 'OK' };
};
```

